# Use the image CMD instead of replacing it with `sleep infinity`.
#
# The Dockerfile CMD runs hs-start.sh, which starts sshd in the background then
# execs `sleep infinity`, so:
#   * sshd (:22) is ALREADY RUNNING when the agent starts — the service probe
#     and the ssh/pam behavioural probes exercise a live daemon;
#   * PID 1 is `sleep infinity`, so restarting sshd cannot kill the container.
#
# Consequence for solutions: sshd effective config is read from
# /etc/ssh/sshd_config via `sshd -T`, so editing the file suffices for the
# config checks; a restart (if performed) is safe.
